## Notes on the schedule

**Erg handover:** C & D start their warm-up 10 min after A & B (programStartOffset: 600s), so they're ready when A & B finish. The pieces then alternate precisely: A & B piece → C & D piece → A & B piece + 4-min rest → C & D piece, etc. Rest intervals for each pair *are* the time the other pair is rowing.

**Technique drills:** One rower at a time; the coach runs all four serially in one 12-minute step (3 min × 4). A & B's drill reps (instances: count 2, serial) represent A then B; C & D's same structure follows after A & B finish.

**Coach timeline:** Briefs 0–5 min, calls splits during the first three pieces (22–42 min), runs drills 40–52 min (concurrent with final pieces and first drills), debriefs after cooldown finishes.

**Cooldown together:** Both pairs floor work at the same time (task: floor, maxConcurrent: 4).

